<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">English Tangier</h1><p class="st-meta">1661 CE – 1684 CE · capital Tangier</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Tangier under English rule after it came as part of Catherine of Braganza's dowry, a costly garrison abandoned after twenty-two years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1661 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-england">Charles II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England</a> as part of the dowry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-of-braganza">Catherine of Braganza</a>. English troops took over in January 1662, hoping to make it a naval base controlling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-gibraltar">Strait of Gibraltar</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a> was governed by military governors such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-rutherford-1st-earl-of-teviot">Earl of Teviot</a>, who was killed in an ambush in 1664. The English built a great mole to create a harbour and granted the town a municipal charter in 1668. The garrison was under constant pressure from Moroccan forces, especially after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moulay-ismail">Moulay Ismail</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alaouite-sultanate">Alaouite Sultanate</a> came to power.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>With costs rising and Parliament unwilling to pay, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-england">Charles II</a> ordered the evacuation. In 1684 the English blew up the mole and fortifications, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-pepys">Samuel Pepys</a> among the officials present, and left the town to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-morocco">Morocco</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/english-tangier.jpg" alt="English Tangier" width="320" height="236"><figcaption>Image: Leonardo de Ferrari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Planta_de_Tanger,_Leonardo_de_Ferrari,_1655.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1661 CE – 1684 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tangier</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles II, Earl of Teviot</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tangier (English)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1672&amp;focus=english-tangier" aria-label="English Tangier on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4534 886 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where English Tangier lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4854 1142L4866 1138M4854 1142L4970 663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4866 1138h0M4970 663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4854 1142h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4854 1142h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tangier. <a href="/atlas?year=1672&amp;focus=english-tangier">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
